-- title:
--   Conjugated Gauss ring restricts to the floor valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M' \ge 1$ be an integer with $q \nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota_0 : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota_0(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K \subseteq L(\!(X)\!)$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-field of ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the unit-reduction map out of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ given by `ZMod.unitsMap (dvd_sq_mul q M')`, and let $K_0 \subseteq L(\!(X)\!)$ be the corresponding $L$-subfield built from level $\Gamma_0(M')$, with $K_0 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ that can be written as a ratio $x/y$ of power series over $A$ whose denominator has nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal, and let $O_0$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ defined by the same condition. Let $\tau : \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \to \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ be such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the automorphism $\tau(\gamma)$ satisfies `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') (levelH q M') γ⁻¹`: whenever $f,g$ are modular forms of weight $k$ and level $\Gamma_H$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g \ne 0$, and $x \in K$ has Laurent series the image of $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$, then for any $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$ one has $\iota_*(\tau(\gamma)x) \cdot q\text{-}\mathrm{exp}(g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}) = q\text{-}\mathrm{exp}(f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})$. Then for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $K$ regarded as a $K_0$-algebra via the inclusion, an element $x \in K_0$ has its image in $K$ lying in the preimage of $W_0$ under $\tau(\gamma)$ if and only if $x \in O_0$; that is, the conjugated Gauss ring $\tau(\gamma)^{-1}(W_0)$ cuts out exactly $O_0$ on $K_0$.
--
--   The statement says that the valuation ring of $K$ obtained from the Gauss ring $W_0$ by conjugating with a level automorphism $\tau(\gamma)$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, still lies over the floor ring $O_0$ of the smaller function field $K_0$ of level $\Gamma_0(M')$. It is used in the analysis of the branch orbit of the full-level covering, feeding the study of the image of the $j$-chart in the supersingular set.
